# Commercial S12.1 runtime lifecycle review diagnosis

- Scope: final same-SHA review of the bounded S12.1 runtime controller.
- Finding 1: controlled safe-stop was invoked by the controller after the
  credential-bearing oneshot transaction had ended.
- Finding 2: rollback discarded the result of `systemctl stop` and could write
  a successful rollback marker without proving the unit inactive.
- Correction 1: safe-stop is now `ExecStartPost` in the same systemd service
  transaction; the controller validates its retained controlled-inactive
  evidence before removing the runtime contract.
- Correction 2: rollback stops every non-inactive unit, checks the command
  result, and requires `ActiveState=inactive` plus `SubState=dead` before any
  restoration or success marker.
- Failure posture: either lifecycle proof failing aborts fail-closed. No second
  deployment attempt, secret handling change, provider expansion, or server
  mutation is introduced by this source correction.
- Rollback: restore the prior reviewed Control commit; no runtime attempt has
  yet occurred.
